s10-2-p10 = prose (cons "To construct \(\lambda\), split the fold into the prefix before \(i\), the element \(v_i\), and the suffix after \(i\). Associativity and commutativity of modular addition and additive inverses cancel \(v_i\) and insert \(x\). The result is an inhabitant of \(\mathsf{Mat}(q,u_{i,x}(v))\), computed from one old element and two modular operations rather than by refolding the vector. Publishing the edited vector under a new immutable identity selects this maintained result for a subscribed sum view. If a subsequent transformation gives \(\theta:q=q'\), the same \(r'\) becomes a maintained result for \(q'\) through \(e'\cdot\mathsf{ap}(\lambda f.f(v'),\theta)\). A local compiled artifact or a remote evaluator can consume the resulting definition and value at the same type. Device reads that supply later edits remain separate world interactions; reuse of the pure sum does not repeat them." nil)
